{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/442796-spirit-sense-seeing-across-the-gauntlet-at-will","id":442796,"title":"Spirit Sense - seeing across the gauntlet at will","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-15T10:38:19-07:00","id":442796,"title":"Spirit Sense - seeing across the gauntlet at will","content":"<br /> So this came up in my game last night. An Urathra in human form is standing outside a sorority house. He decides to use his spirit sense to check things out in the Shadow before knocking. <br /> <br /> Not having read the book cover to cover yet, I had to go look up spirit sense, which is mercifully brief and to the point: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Uratha are Uratha thanks to their connection to the world <br /> of Spirit. They\u2019re attuned to the Shadow, and can peek across <br /> to experience it, extending any or all of their senses across the <br /> Gauntlet. </div> </div> </div>I pressed through, per ST fashion, but had a question:<br /> <br /> *How does he appear when doing this? Zoned out? Ten thousand foot stare? Is he utterly unaware of what's going on around him in the regular world while doing this? (Could that be a vulnerability?) Even if he just chose to 'split' his senses between the Shadow and the real world, it'd be distracting.<br /> *Does anything in the Shadow know or notice him while doing this? Might they if they were paying attention? <br /> *Does the strength of the gauntlet influence anything? <br /> <br /> This action seems like a reaching action, but it says they can pretty much do it at will. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T11:09:23-07:00","id":442829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf the Forsaken 2nd edition &quot;p.94&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>With an instant action to focus, the Uratha can send any of<br /> her senses across the Gauntlet. If she wishes to do so reflexively, she<br /> must spend a point of Essence</b>. This can extend her human or wolf<br /> senses across in either direction. Each of her sensesis binary; she can<br /> see or smell or hear in either spirit or flesh. <b>If she<br /> sends some but not all of her senses to the Shadow, she suffers a \u20132<br /> penalty to all actions that rely on Perception or concentration, and<br /> loses her ability to ignore sensory penalties from her wolf senses.</b><br /> A werewolf can only send her form\u2019s default senses across the<br /> Gauntlet \u2014 she cannot pass her wolf\u2019s sense of smell to the Hisil in<br /> Dalu form. <b>The Gauntlet poses a further barrier; her Perception<br /> rolls suffer a penalty determined by the Gauntlet\u2019s strength</b> (p. 101)<br /> The werewolf does not need to focus in order to sense spirits<br /> in Twilight. Unless the spirit is intentionally trying to hide,<br /> Uratha sense spirits in Twilight as well as they would manifested</div> </div> </div> </div>Is easily missed as the pages 94 and 95 are flipped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T11:26:47-07:00","id":442857,"title":"","content":"Exactly what I needed, thanks. From the flavor text I'll assume spirits can sense uratha pretty much at will too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}